---

<PageLayout title='About' {headings}>
  <p>
    Hi, I'm <strong>Javier Cacheiro López</strong> — you may know me as
    <code>javicacheiro</code>. I'm a PhD working at
    <a href='https://www.cesga.es' target='_blank'>CESGA</a> (Galicia Supercomputing Center) in
    Santiago de Compostela, Spain, where I lead the Big Data team and serve as Scientific Director
    of the <a href='https://dataspace.cesga.es' target='_blank'>OneHealth DataSpace</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    I'm passionate about technology and science, and I've spent my career at the intersection of
    both: making supercomputers, big data platforms and cloud infrastructures useful for
    researchers and companies.
  </p>

  <h2 id='what-i-do'>What I Do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Scientific Director, OneHealth DataSpace</strong> — leading the scientific vision of a
      sovereign data space for health, animal and environmental data built on CESGA's
      supercomputing infrastructure.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Big Data team lead at CESGA</strong> — running the Big Data infrastructure and
      services of the Galicia Supercomputing Center.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>HPC &amp; Cloud</strong> — helping science and industry get the most out of
      high-performance computing and cloud platforms.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id='onehealth-dataspace'>OneHealth DataSpace</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href='https://dataspace.cesga.es' target='_blank'>OneHealth DataSpace</a> goes beyond
    data sharing: it lets organizations <em>share</em> data with sovereignty (controlled access and
    conditions), <em>analyze</em> it with Big Data tools, <em>compute</em> on CESGA's
    supercomputing resources (simulations, AI training, genomics), and <em>expose</em> the results
    as APIs, dashboards or applications. It is funded by the Spanish Ministry for Digital
    Transformation through NextGenerationEU.
  </p>

  <h2 id='topics'>Topics I Write About</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>HPC</strong> — supercomputing, schedulers, performance</li>
    <li><strong>Quantum Computing</strong> — where quantum meets HPC</li>
    <li><strong>AI</strong> — training and serving models on real infrastructure</li>
    <li><strong>Big Data</strong> — data engineering at scale</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud</strong> — cloud platforms and infrastructure automation</li>
    <li><strong>Data Spaces</strong> — sovereign data sharing between organizations</li>
  </ul>

